{
  "id": "focal-attention",
  "term": "focal attention",
  "definition": "Focal attention is a later, more concentrated mode of visual processing centered on the fovea that supports identifying objects and understanding their meaning. In eye-movement research, it is typically associated with longer fixations and shorter saccades than the broader, spatially orienting ambient mode.",
